# Line endings are part of the quality gate contract.
#
# Without this file the working tree's line endings depend on each developer's
# `core.autocrlf`. On a Windows checkout with `autocrlf=true` every tracked text
# file lands as CRLF, and `npm run format:check` — which Prettier runs with its
# default `endOfLine: "lf"` — fails on the whole tree even though the committed
# content is byte-identical to what CI checks. The same gate must produce the
# same result on every machine, so the working tree is normalised to LF.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts are consumed by PowerShell and cmd, which expect CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# The Gradle wrapper is executed by two different shells.
gradlew text eol=lf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted or diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
*.p8 binary
*.p12 binary
*.mobileprovision binary
*.tar binary
*.dump binary
